claimed: channel-seam — the operator's design, and it is better than replacing the mechanism in place: make Channel an INTERFACE with swappable implementations, so a ring, a relaxed FIFO and a MultiFIFO can each arrive in their own lane, be measured against each other and against zio.Queue, instead of one rewrite that must be all-or-nothing (channel-ring's integration deadlocked precisely because it had to replace the mechanism wholesale). This lane is the SEAM ONLY, zero behaviour change: trait Channel[A] carrying the primitives, the current STM implementation moved behind it unchanged as StmChannel, and Channel.apply as the factory -- which keeps all 73 existing construction sites compiling untouched, since Channel[A](capacity) is already an apply. Implementations follow in their own lanes. Note for the interface's honesty: STM composability (Tx.read on the channel's own cell, which TestStm exercises) is a property of the STM implementation and CANNOT be promised by the interface, since a ring-backed channel has no such cell.
